<section class="section shell overview" id="overview" aria-labelledby="overview-title"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">01 / A LITTLE CONTEXT</p><span class="section-aside">ENGINEERING QUESTIONS. REAL-WORLD CONSEQUENCES.</span></div><div class="overview-grid"><div><h2 id="overview-title">One background.<br><span class="text-muted">Connected perspectives.</span></h2><p class="section-lead">Research asks better questions.<br>Experience keeps them grounded.</p><div class="segmented" role="group" aria-label="Choose an introduction" hidden><button type="button" data-perspective="research" aria-pressed="true">For research & conferences</button><button type="button" data-perspective="professional" aria-pressed="false">For professional opportunities</button></div></div><div class="perspective" id="perspective" aria-live="polite"><div data-perspective-panel="research"><p class="overview-statement">I’m a transport engineer and doctoral researcher exploring <strong>freight accessibility, infrastructure constraints and economic connectivity.</strong></p><p>At Warsaw University of Technology, I combine transport modelling with engineering analysis to understand where freight systems fall short—and how to evaluate improvements.</p><a href="#publications" class="text-link">Explore publications & conference contributions <span>↗</span></a></div><div data-perspective-panel="professional"><p class="overview-statement">I bring an engineering approach to <strong>analysis, operational delivery and clear communication.</strong></p><p>Alongside research and university teaching, my experience at Accenture covers accounts receivable, reporting, escalations, month-end support and training colleagues. I’m comfortable moving between detailed analysis and the people who need to use it.</p><a href="#experience" class="text-link">Explore my professional background <span>↗</span></a></div></div></div><div class="evidence-grid"><div><span class="evidence-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><h3>Research & publication</h3><p>Transport systems, accessibility and engineering methods.</p></div><div><span class="evidence-icon blue" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><h3>Simulation & analysis</h3><p>From network-level modelling to corridor microsimulation.</p></div><div><span class="evidence-icon warm" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><h3>Teaching & operations</h3><p>Technical communication, reporting and practical delivery.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="research-section" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title"><div class="section shell"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">02 / THE RESEARCH</p><span class="section-aside">MAKING THE INVISIBLE VISIBLE</span></div><div class="section-heading-grid"><h2 id="research-title">A road can exist.<br><span class="accent-text">Access can still be missing.</span></h2><p class="section-lead">A business may be connected to the road network and still struggle to receive goods reliably or affordably. That gap is the starting point for my doctoral work.</p></div><div class="research-thesis"><div class="thesis-index"><span class="tiny">DOCTORAL RESEARCH</span><span class="thesis-line" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="tiny">2024 → ONGOING</span></div><div><h3>Transport poverty in freight transportation networks</h3><p>How can freight disadvantage be measured and reduced through engineering analysis?</p><div class="thesis-meta"><span>Warsaw University of Technology · Faculty of Transport</span><span>Supervisor: Prof. Mariusz Kostrzewski</span></div></div></div>
<div class="explorer" data-explorer-mode="access"><div class="explorer-left"><span class="eyebrow">THE IDEA, IN PLAIN LANGUAGE</span><h3>Look beyond<br>the route.</h3><p>Explore three questions behind a freight connection.</p><div class="explorer-controls" role="group" aria-label="Explore freight accessibility" hidden><button type="button" data-network="access" aria-pressed="true"><span>01</span> Can goods get there? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button type="button" data-network="traffic" aria-pressed="false"><span>02</span> What slows them down? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button type="button" data-network="reliability" aria-pressed="false"><span>03</span> Can delivery be relied on? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div><noscript><p>Freight access depends on usable routes, traffic conditions and reliable services.</p></noscript></div><div class="explorer-right"><svg viewBox="0 0 600 275" class="explorer-art" role="img" aria-label="Conceptual freight network connecting a logistics hub to a business through a constrained route"><defs><pattern id="explorer-grid" width="25" height="25" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><circle cx="1" cy="1" r=".8" class="svg-grid"/></pattern></defs><rect width="600" height="275" fill="url(#explorer-grid)"/><g class="network-ghost" fill="none"><path d="M0 60H180L280 160H410L520 50H600M0 205H180L250 135H385L470 220H600M100 0V90L220 210V275M380 0V85L470 175V275"/></g><path class="explore-route" d="M90 155H175L265 65H360L450 155H520" fill="none"/><path class="explore-alternative" d="M175 155L265 245H360L450 155" fill="none"/><path class="explore-constraint" d="M267 65H358" fill="none"/><g class="explore-node"><circle cx="90" cy="155" r="11"/><circle cx="520" cy="155" r="11"/><circle cx="175" cy="155" r="6"/><circle cx="450" cy="155" r="6"/></g><g class="explore-label"><text x="42" y="194">LOGISTICS HUB</text><text x="478" y="194">BUSINESS</text><text x="265" y="42" class="constraint-label">ROAD CONSTRAINT</text></g><g class="moving-particle"><circle r="4" fill="var(--accent)"><animateMotion dur="7s" repeatCount="indefinite" path="M90 155H175L265 65H360L450 155H520"/></circle></g><g class="traffic-particles"><circle cx="300" cy="65" r="6"/><circle cx="320" cy="65" r="6"/><circle cx="340" cy="65" r="6"/></g></svg><div class="explorer-copy" aria-live="polite"><span class="tag" id="explorer-tag">NETWORK ACCESSIBILITY</span><h4 id="explorer-title">Connected doesn’t always mean accessible.</h4><p id="explorer-description">Road geometry, pavement condition or service gaps can make a connection harder to use. My research examines how these constraints should be represented in freight accessibility measures.</p></div><p class="diagram-disclaimer">Conceptual illustration. These views explain research questions; they do not show measured or simulated results.</p></div></div>
<div class="projects-top"><h3>Research in motion<span class="accent-text">.</span></h3><span class="tiny">EXPAND A PROJECT TO EXPLORE</span></div><div class="project-grid">
<details class="project"><summary><span class="project-kicker"><i class="project-dot mint"></i> CURRENT RESEARCH · WARSAW</span><h4>Passenger traffic.<br>Freight consequences.</h4><p>Investigating how mixed traffic affects freight delay and reliability.</p><span class="project-bottom">VISSIM · CORRIDOR MODELLING <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span></span></summary><div class="project-detail"><h5>The question</h5><p>How does passenger demand affect freight performance on shared urban roads?</p><h5>What’s done</h5><p>An exploratory Modlińska–Elektronowa corridor pilot was presented at LSTP in September 2026.</p><h5>What’s next</h5><p>The awarded WUT grant, “Freight Transport Penalty under Mixed-Traffic Conditions, Including the Context of Undesirable Emissions: A Microsimulation Approach,” supports the next stage of corridor modelling and empirical analysis.</p><span class="small-note">The pilot is not a validated city-wide result.</span></div></details>
<details class="project"><summary><span class="project-kicker"><i class="project-dot blue"></i> METHODOLOGY · IN DEVELOPMENT</span><h4>Putting freight<br>disadvantage into focus.</h4><p>Developing an accessibility-based approach to freight transport poverty.</p><span class="project-bottom">ACCESSIBILITY · INDICATORS <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span></span></summary><div class="project-detail"><h5>The question</h5><p>What does transport disadvantage mean for freight actors, and how can it be measured defensibly?</p><h5>Current direction</h5><p>Candidate dimensions include network accessibility, logistics-service availability and reliability, and economic accessibility. The formulation remains open to revision.</p><h5>What’s next</h5><p>Compare candidate measures with simpler baselines and test sensitivity, uncertainty and added explanatory value.</p><span class="small-note">Conceptual development and empirical validation are ongoing.</span></div></details>
<details class="project"><summary><span class="project-kicker"><i class="project-dot warm"></i> PUBLISHED CASE STUDY · ABU DHABI</span><h4>Real traffic.<br>Testable alternatives.</h4><p>Using digital shadowing to investigate the 79th Street corridor in Musaffah.</p><span class="project-bottom">VISSIM · DIGITAL SHADOWING <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span></span></summary><div class="project-detail"><h5>The approach</h5><p>Model and calibrate an urban corridor using manually collected peak and off-peak traffic observations, then evaluate congestion and proposed alternatives.</p><h5>The output</h5><p>Published in Transportation Research Procedia, volume 93, pages 826–832 (2026), following TRANSCOM 2025.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.trpro.2025.12.010" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the publication <span>↗</span></a></div></details>
<details class="project"><summary><span class="project-kicker"><i class="project-dot violet"></i> WORKING PAPER · IN REVISION</span><h4>The quality<br>behind the connection.</h4><p>Exploring how pavement and geometric constraints affect freight accessibility.</p><span class="project-bottom">INFRASTRUCTURE · EIGHT CORRIDORS <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span></span></summary><div class="project-detail"><h5>The approach</h5><p>A preliminary assessment of eight Warsaw freight corridors combines accessibility measures with pavement condition and geometric constraints.</p><h5>The purpose</h5><p>Investigate how engineering quality changes the interpretation of network access and could inform intervention priorities.</p><span class="small-note">Exploratory study; further empirical testing of the proposed indicators is planned.</span></div></details>
</div></div></section>
<section class="section shell" id="publications" aria-labelledby="publications-title"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">03 / SELECTED WORK</p><a class="text-link" href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=lB2_-wEAAAAJ&amp;hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="section-heading-grid"><h2 id="publications-title">Work that’s<br><span class="text-muted">out in the world.</span></h2><p class="section-lead">Published research, conference contributions and forthcoming work. Each record shows where it stands.</p></div><div class="publication-tools" hidden><div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter research outputs"><button type="button" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All work <span>06</span></button><button type="button" data-filter="Published" aria-pressed="false">Published <span>03</span></button><button type="button" data-filter="other" aria-pressed="false">Presented & forthcoming <span>03</span></button></div><label class="search-box"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="5.5"/><path d="m13 13 4 4"/></svg><span class="sr-only">Search publications by title, topic or venue</span><input id="publication-search" type="search" placeholder="Search a topic, title or venue" autocomplete="off"></label></div><p class="sr-only" id="filter-status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="works">{% for work in portfolio.works %}<article class="work" data-status="{{ work.status }}"><div class="work-number">0{{ loop.index }}</div><div class="work-content"><div class="work-meta"><span>{{ work.type }}</span><span class="status status-{{ work.status | lower }}">{{ work.status }}</span></div><h3>{% if work.url %}<a href="{{ work.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ work.title }} <span class="inline-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% else %}{{ work.title }}{% endif %}</h3><p class="venue">{{ work.