<section class="experience-section" id="experience" aria-labelledby="experience-title"><div class="section shell"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">04 / EXPERIENCE & PERSPECTIVE</p><a class="text-link" href="/profile/">Print-friendly profile <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="section-heading-grid"><h2 id="experience-title">Analytical by training.<br><span class="accent-text">Practical by experience.</span></h2><p class="section-lead">Engineering, research, teaching and finance operations have shaped how I work: understand the system, investigate the detail, communicate clearly.</p></div><div class="experience-layout"><div class="experience-note"><div class="abstract-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div><h3>Different contexts.<br>The same curiosity.</h3><p>I’m interested in how systems work—and how careful analysis can make them work better for the people who depend on them.</p><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ahmed-madhoun/" class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Professional profile on LinkedIn <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="experience-list"><article><div class="role-label"><span>WARSAW UNIVERSITY OF TECHNOLOGY</span><span class="tag">RESEARCH & TEACHING</span></div><h3>Transport research.<br>Technical communication.</h3><p>Doctoral research at the Faculty of Transport, alongside university teaching experience in engineering graphics and descriptive geometry.</p><div class="skill-chips"><span>Research design</span><span>Transport modelling</span><span>University teaching</span></div></article><article><div class="role-label"><span>ACCENTURE</span><span class="tag tag-blue">FINANCE OPERATIONS EXPERIENCE</span></div><h3>Detail, accountability<br>and operational delivery.</h3><p>Accounts receivable and cash collections experience covering reporting, escalations and month-end support, with responsibilities in training new colleagues and Excel training.</p><div class="skill-chips"><span>AR & collections</span><span>Operational reporting</span><span>Training & support</span></div></article><article><div class="role-label"><span>ENGINEERING FOUNDATION</span><span class="tag tag-warm">EDUCATION & METHODS</span></div><h3>From infrastructure<br>to network performance.</h3><p>A civil engineering foundation, a master’s degree in Transport Systems Engineering and Management at Warsaw University of Technology, including transport network modelling with PTV Visum, and subsequent microscopic simulation of urban corridors with PTV Vissim.</p><div class="skill-chips"><span>PTV Visum</span><span>PTV Vissim</span><span>Engineering analysis</span></div></article></div></div><div class="toolbox"><span class="eyebrow">TOOLS & METHODS</span><div><span>PTV Vissim</span><span>PTV Visum</span><span>Excel & reporting</span><span>Accessibility analysis</span><span>Scenario modelling</span><span>Technical writing</span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section shell" id="activity" aria-labelledby="activity-title"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">05 / BEYOND THE DESK</p><span class="section-aside">PRESENTING. EXCHANGING. BUILDING.</span></div><div class="activity-grid"><div><h2 id="activity-title">Research is<br><span class="text-muted">a conversation.</span></h2><p class="section-lead">Conference contributions connect the work to other researchers, new questions and different ways of seeing the same problem.</p><div class="recognition-card"><span class="recognition-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><div><span class="tiny">RECOGNITION & SUPPORT</span><h3>2026 WUT scientific competition recognition</h3><p>Plus an awarded 2026–2027 research grant on passenger-induced freight penalties under mixed-traffic conditions.</p></div></div></div><ol class="conference-list"><li><span class="conference-year">2026</span><div><h3>LSTP</h3><p>Jachranka · September 2026</p><span>Passenger–freight interactions and corridor microsimulation.</span></div><span class="conference-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></li><li><span class="conference-year">2026</span><div><h3>TRANSBALTICA</h3><p>September 2026</p><span>Accessibility-based assessment of freight transport poverty.</span></div><span class="conference-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></li><li><span class="conference-year">2025</span><div><h3>Transport XXI Wieku</h3><p>Conference contribution</p><span>Smart planning, reconstruction and freight accessibility.</span></div><span class="conference-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></li><li><span class="conference-year">2025</span><div><h3>TRANSCOM</h3><p>Conference contribution</p><span>Simulation-based alternatives for Musaffah’s 79th Street.</span></div><span class="conference-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="agenda-section" id="agenda" aria-labelledby="agenda-title"><div class="section shell"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">06 / WHAT COMES NEXT</p><span class="section-aside">RESEARCH AGENDA · 2026–2028</span></div><div class="section-heading-grid"><h2 id="agenda-title">Better questions.<br><span class="accent-text">Stronger evidence.</span></h2><p class="section-lead">The next phase turns an established research direction into a tested contribution. These are planned objectives, with validation still ahead.</p></div><ol class="agenda-items"><li><span class="agenda-node">01</span><span class="tiny">2026–2027</span><h3>Build the evidence.</h3><p>Expand corridor datasets, record data provenance, calibrate selected Warsaw models and refine research questions.</p><span class="agenda-tag">DATA → MODELS</span></li><li><span class="agenda-node">02</span><span class="tiny">2027</span><h3>Test what holds.</h3><p>Validate models, compare candidate indicators against baseline methods and examine performance across corridor scenarios.</p><span class="agenda-tag">MODELS → INSIGHT</span></li><li><span class="agenda-node">03</span><span class="tiny">2027–2028</span><h3>Connect the findings.</h3><p>Assess uncertainty and sensitivity, integrate results and develop the doctoral synthesis. Submission is targeted for September 2028.</p><span class="agenda-tag">INSIGHT → CONTRIBUTION</span></li></ol></div></section>
